{"code":"var __defProp=Object.defineProperty;var __name=(target,value)=>__defProp(target,\"name\",{value,configurable:true});import{z}from\"zod\";import{defineTool}from\"@papercusp/agent-mcp\";import{resolveAgentIdentity}from\"../coordination/identity\";import{COORD_ROLES}from\"../coordination/roles\";import{sendMessage}from\"../coordination/messages\";import{mergeIds,runBulk,bulkContent}from\"@papercusp/agent-mcp/_bulk\";var drain_default=defineTool({name:\"fleet:drain\",description:\"Signal one OR many running bees to gracefully wind down (checkpoint, release locks/claims, return work-list, exit). Pass `bee_id` for one or `bee_ids` for several. Distinct from fleet:cancel (hard kill). The bee can cooperate or request deferral (propose/dispose); the Queen waits bounded time before reclaiming the slot. Returns immediately; the drain is async. Returns { ok, results:[{ ok, bee_id, msg_id, \\u2026 | error }], counts } \\u2014 correlate by bee_id, not position; one failure never fails the rest.\",guidance:{when:\"You (the Queen) want to reclaim bee slot(s): the occupant has low-priority work, is blocked, or the priorities have shifted. Send a drain cue to give each bee a chance to hand off cleanly. Reclaiming several at once? Pass them all via `bee_ids`.\",notWhen:\"The bee is actively running a high-priority task (let it finish naturally). Or if immediate slot reclaim is critical (use fleet:cancel). Or if the bee is unresponsive (use fleet:cancel after a timeout).\",chaining:\"fleet:drain { bee_id } | { bee_ids:[\\u2026] } \\u2192 (later, bounded) fleet:assignments { agent: bee_id } \\u2192 fleet:spawn fresh. Bulk: correlate by bee_id, not position; one failure never fails the rest.\"},capability:\"coord:write\",requirePrincipal:false,agentRoles:[...COORD_ROLES],args:z.object({bee_id:z.string().min(1).optional().describe(\"Owner ID of one bee to drain (spawn_id or session id; n=1 shorthand for bee_ids:[id]).\"),bee_ids:z.array(z.string().min(1)).min(1).max(100).optional